{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Have you not made a hedge about him</b> — From לשיכים in your eyes [= as you see it]. Remove his hedge and it becomes a devastation. Its meaning: you have hedged about him, like: a vineyard's hedge, so that no harm touch it." "<b>Burst forth</b> — Increased, like: ופרצת ימה וקדמה (Genesis 28:14)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The Hebrew quotes the phrase שכת בעדו from the verse; the parenthetical 'in your eyes' renders בעיניכם, addressed to the Adversary."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:27.519554100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}